 {:name "Host thread grant",
  :unstable false,
  :declarations
  [{:kind :function,
    :name "mino_set_thread_limit",
    :return-type "void",
    :params "mino_state_t *S, int n",
    :signature "void mino_set_thread_limit(mino_state_t *S, int n);",
    :doc
    "Set the per-state thread limit. n=0 or n=1 disables host threads;\nn>1 grants the runtime permission to spawn that many concurrent\nworker threads. Calling with the same value twice is a no-op.\n\nCalling with n>1 BEFORE any `(future ...)` is in flight is the\nsupported sequence; lowering the limit while threads are running\ndoes not interrupt them, but new spawns will respect the new ceiling."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_get_thread_limit",
    :return-type "int",
    :params "mino_state_t *S",
    :signature "int  mino_get_thread_limit(mino_state_t *S);",
    :doc
    "Read the current thread limit. Returns 1 by default (single-threaded)."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_thread_count",
    :return-type "int",
    :params "mino_state_t *S",
    :signature "int  mino_thread_count(mino_state_t *S);",
    :doc
    "Return the count of host threads currently spawned by this state.\nDecremented as threads complete and join. Returns 0 in single-\nthreaded mode."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_quiesce_threads",
    :return-type "void",
    :params "mino_state_t *S",
    :signature "void mino_quiesce_threads(mino_state_t *S);",
    :doc
    "Wait for all in-flight host threads to finish. Intended to be called\nby the embedder before `mino_state_free`; calling it from a worker\nthread that this state spawned is undefined behaviour. Safe to call\nwhen no threads are in flight (returns immediately)."}]}
 {:name "Host thread pool, factory, stack-size knobs",
  :unstable true,
  :declarations
  [{:kind :struct,
    :name "mino_thread_pool_t",
    :fields [{:type "void *", :name "user_data", :comment nil}],
    :struct-tag "mino_thread_pool",
    :doc
    "Function-pointer interface a host thread pool implements. Mino\ncalls submit_fn for each `(future ...)` while a pool is registered;\nthe pool MUST eventually call (*work)(ctx) on a worker thread. The\npool MUST NOT call work synchronously on the calling thread —\nthat defeats the parallelism mino is asking for.",
    :unstable true}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_set_thread_pool",
    :return-type "void",
    :params "mino_state_t *S, mino_thread_pool_t *pool",
    :signature
    "void mino_set_thread_pool(mino_state_t *S, mino_thread_pool_t *pool);",
    :doc
    "Register a host thread pool for this state. Pass NULL to revert\nto spawn-per-future. The pool's `submit_fn` is consulted for each\n`(future ...)`. The pool may be shared across multiple states; mino\ndoes not enforce single-state ownership. The thread_limit still\napplies — submission is rejected when the per-state count is full.",
    :unstable true}
   {:kind :typedef-fn,
    :name "mino_thread_lifecycle_fn",
    :return-type "void",
    :params "mino_state_t *S, void *ctx",
    :signature
    "typedef void (*mino_thread_lifecycle_fn)(mino_state_t *S, void *ctx);",
    :doc
    "Per-thread factory hooks for the spawn-per-future path. start_fn\nruns on the worker thread before the body executes; end_fn runs\nafter the body returns (whether normally or via uncaught throw).\nctx is opaque to mino. Pass NULL fns to clear. Ignored entirely\nwhen a pool is registered (the pool owns thread lifecycle).",
    :unstable true}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_set_thread_factory",
