 {:name "Garbage collector control",
  :unstable true,
  :declarations
  [{:kind :enum,
    :name "mino_gc_kind_t",
    :variants
    [{:name "MINO_GC_MINOR", :comment nil}
     {:name "MINO_GC_MAJOR", :comment nil}
     {:name "MINO_GC_FULL", :comment nil}],
    :doc
    "UNSTABLE: GC tuning, kind enum, phase constants, and the stats\nstruct are provisional. The collector is still evolving\n(generational + incremental layout, threshold heuristics) and this\nsection will track those changes. Pin behavior through explicit\nmino_gc_collect calls at quiescent points; do not rely on tuning\nparameter ranges or the stats struct layout across releases.\n\nKinds of collection the host can request. Use at quiescent points such\nas between REPL turns, after bulk import, or before long-idle periods.\n\nMINO_GC_MINOR -- nursery collection only; cheapest, bounded by young set\nsize. Safe at any time including mid-major.\nMINO_GC_MAJOR -- drain any in-flight incremental major cycle and sweep,\nthen start a fresh STW major if no cycle is active.\nReclaims old-gen dead; leaves young-gen alone.\nMINO_GC_FULL  -- minor, then finish or run a fresh STW major.\nStrongest reclamation; highest pause.",
    :unstable true}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_gc_collect",
    :return-type "void",
    :params "mino_state_t *S, mino_gc_kind_t kind",
    :signature
    "void mino_gc_collect(mino_state_t *S, mino_gc_kind_t kind);",
    :doc nil,
    :unstable true}
   {:kind :enum,
    :name "mino_gc_param_t",
    :variants
    [{:name "MINO_GC_NURSERY_BYTES", :comment nil}
     {:name "MINO_GC_MAJOR_GROWTH_TENTHS", :comment nil}
     {:name "MINO_GC_PROMOTION_AGE", :comment nil}
     {:name "MINO_GC_INCREMENTAL_BUDGET", :comment nil}
     {:name "MINO_GC_STEP_ALLOC_BYTES", :comment nil}],
    :doc
    "Tunable parameters. Values out of range are rejected; mino_gc_set_param\nreturns 0 on success and -1 on a bad parameter or out-of-range value.\n\nNURSERY_BYTES       young-gen trigger; minor fires when young exceeds.\nDefault 1 MiB. Range 64 KiB .. 256 MiB.\nMAJOR_GROWTH_TENTHS old-gen growth multiplier in tenths (15 = 1.5x).\nDefault 15. Range 11 .. 40.\nPROMOTION_AGE       minor-survival count before YOUNG->OLD promotion.\nDefault 1. Range 1 .. 8.\nINCREMENTAL_BUDGET  headers popped per incremental major slice.\nDefault 4096. Range 64 .. 65536.\nSTEP_ALLOC_BYTES    bytes allocated between automatic slices.\nDefault 16 KiB. Range 1 KiB .. 16 MiB.",
    :unstable true}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_gc_set_param",
    :return-type "int",
    :params "mino_state_t *S, mino_gc_param_t p, size_t value",
    :signature
    "int mino_gc_set_param(mino_state_t *S, mino_gc_param_t p, size_t value);",
    :doc nil,
    :unstable true}
   {:kind :define,
    :name "MINO_GC_PHASE_IDLE",
    :value "0",
    :inline-comment nil,
    :signature "#define MINO_GC_PHASE_IDLE        0",
    :doc "Phase tag returned in mino_gc_stats_t.phase.",
    :unstable true}
   {:kind :define,
    :name "MINO_GC_PHASE_MINOR",
    :value "1",
    :inline-comment nil,
    :signature "#define MINO_GC_PHASE_MINOR       1",
    :doc nil,
    :unstable true}
   {:kind :define,
    :name "MINO_GC_PHASE_MAJOR_MARK",
    :value "2",
    :inline-comment nil,
    :signature "#define MINO_GC_PHASE_MAJOR_MARK  2",
    :doc nil,
    :unstable true}
   {:kind :define,
    :name "MINO_GC_PHASE_MAJOR_SWEEP",
    :value "3",
    :inline-comment nil,
    :signature "#define MINO_GC_PHASE_MAJOR_SWEEP 3",
    :doc nil,
    :unstable true}
   {:kind :struct,
    :name "mino_gc_stats_t",
    :fields
    [{:type "size_t", :name "collections_minor", :comment nil}
     {:type "size_t", :name "collections_major", :comment nil}
     {:type "size_t", :name "bytes_live", :comment "young + old"}
     {:type "size_t", :name "bytes_young", :comment nil}
     {:type "size_t", :name "bytes_old", :comment nil}
     {:type "size_t",
      :name "bytes_alloc",
      :comment "current; reset by major, decremented by minor"}
     {:type "size_t",
      :name "bytes_freed",
      :comment "monotonic: total ever swept"}
     {:type "size_t", :name "total_gc_ns", :comment nil}
     {:type "size_t", :name "max_gc_ns", :comment nil}
     {:type "size_t",
      :name "remset_entries",
      :comment "current remembered-set size"}
     {:type "size_t",
      :name "remset_cap",
      :comment "remembered-set capacity"}
     {:type "size_t",
      :name "remset_high_water",
      :comment "peak remset size this state"}
     {:type "size_t",
      :name "mark_stack_cap",
      :comment "mark-stack capacity"}
     {:type "size_t",
      :name "mark_stack_high_water",
      :comment "peak mark-stack depth this state"}
     {:type "int", :name "phase", :comment "MINO_GC_PHASE_*"}],
    :doc
    "Collector statistics. Populated by mino_gc_stats. No allocation is\nperformed; the host owns the out struct. Counters are cumulative\nsince state creation except where noted.\n\nNote: bytes_alloc is NOT a monotonic total. It tracks bytes live in\nthe bump path; minor GC decrements it by the bytes it sweeps and\nmajor GC resets it to bytes_live. To recover a true allocation\ntotal over a window, sum (delta bytes_alloc + delta bytes_freed);\nbytes_freed IS monotonic. This is the formula the perf-gate\nallocation tracker uses.",
    :unstable true}
